    "narrative": "Today\u2019s outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on top-tier leverage, headlined by **James Wood** (75.63) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.10), our most compelling starts. **James Wood** secures the highest score of the day, buoyed by a prime leadoff spot against Mitch Keller; despite Keller\u2019s competence, **James Wood**\u2019s elite xwOBA of 0.418 makes him a lock. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+14%) and a favorable platoon matchup against Logan Webb, highlighting the importance of targeting hitter-friendly environments. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** (72.10) and **Isaac Paredes** (71.63) anchor the infield, both projecting as high-floor plays due to soft matchups against Jose Cabrera and Nick Martinez, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved the final bench spot, where **Edwin Arroyo** (49.84) narrowly missed the cut over **Dalton Rushing** (52.60) and **Alex Freeland** (53.06). While **Edwin Arroyo** benefits from switch-hitting flexibility, his projected #9 spot in the lineup creates a drag on his efficiency score compared to the slightly more favorable positioning of our active middle infielders. Elsewhere, **Josh Naylor** (45.99) was relegated to the bench; despite a strong base projection, he is currently being neutralized by a matchup against an elite arm in Dylan Cease and a poor BvP track record. Owners should monitor the rain risk for **Travis Bazzana** (48.67), whose benching was ultimately sealed by both weather concerns and lower baseline efficiency. With several lineups still pending, managers should keep a close eye on confirmation for **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Brice Turang**, **Alex Freeland**, **Max Muncy**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Henry Bolte**, as any shift out of their projected spots could necessitate a recalibration of today's strategy.",
